  "notes": [
    "Cartridge RTTI names the three classes daTrs_c (_ZTS7daTrs_c), daTBasket_c (_ZTS11daTBasket_c) and daTrsIcon_c (_ZTS11daTrsIcon_c). They interleave through one .text run, so the TU is named for the primary class and carries no '+' in its path.",
    "The licensed run is .text 0x02115ee0..0x0211c600 (97 functions): tu_map's 93-function unit plus the four registry factories that follow it (daTrsIcon_c_classInit, daTBasket_c_classInit, daTrs_c_classInit_BOSS_TERESA, daTrs_c_classInit_TERESA). The next TU starts with daTrsTrap_c's D1 at 0x0211c600.",
    "Each destructor is declared in its class header and defined once, out of line, first in the file. Under #pragma defer_codegen off that emits D1 then D0 in ROM order, plus a homeless D2.",
    "The factories are `return new X()`. This TU emits the vtables, so the vptr store is the emitting-TU spelling; objisolate and reloc_audit accept it as-is.",
    "func_ov063_0211640c needs opt_propagation off (smulbb against an s16 -1 kept in a register). The push/pop bracket has to close after the following definition (021166ac): closing it directly after 0211640c leaves 0211640c unmatched. Deleting the bracket unmatches 0211640c alone. The shards' opt_common_subs off (02116a1c) and optimize_for_size on (02119a50) brackets were deleted: removing either left 97/97.",
    "__sinit_ov063_0211e29c (0x0211e29c) constructs this unit's SharedFilePtrs at bss 0x0211edc4..0x0211edf4 but keeps its own source: a text-only promotion cannot own .init."
  ],
